<title>UK: ALUMINIUM STOCKS RISE IN JUNE - IPAI.</title>
<headline>ALUMINIUM STOCKS RISE IN JUNE - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, rose to 3.056 million tonnes at the end of June 1997, compared with 3.045 million in May and 3.375 million in June 1996, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks rose to 1.571 million tonnes versus 1.549 million and 1.819 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   June 97   May 97   June 96</p>
<p>    Africa		    46	 61	  67</p>
<p>    North America	1,440    1,421     1,630</p>
<p>    Latin America	  143	136	 183</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	151	151	 160</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,144    1,141     1,203</p>
<p>    Oceania		  132	135	 132</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   June 97   May 97   June 96</p>
<p>    Africa		    13	 24	  28</p>
<p>    North America	  608	595	 747</p>
<p>    Latin America	   95	 87	 133</p>
<p>    East/South Asia	109	113	 132</p>
<p>    Europe West	    656	639	 680</p>
<p>    Oceania		   90	 91	  99</p>
</text>
